The Ninth Party System refers to the era of American national politics that began in 2132 with the rise of the [[Union Party (United States)|Union Party]] under [[Lionel Halvidar|Lionel J. Halvidar]]. It followed the Eighth Party System which started under [[Oscar Lachman]]. It continued to the election of 2156 which saw the Union Party merge with the Progress Party which resulted in the [[Tenth Party System]]. The dominant personalities during this period are Presidents Lionel Halvidar (U), Ha-eun Zaya (U), two-time party nominee Anakin F. Johnson (U), and former Party leader Steven Shen (C).

The Ninth Party System was defined by a new form of American nationalism aimed at colonial integration. Economic policy was functionally replaced entirely by the Quantum Economic Model.

